# three.js math classes: the fields whose contents the library never lets be
# anything but numbers. Hand-written against
# tests/oracle/threejs/three/math/*.js — every entry below is a field the class
# body assigns and the whole library only ever assigns numbers to.
#
# A pin is a PROMISE, not a proof (src/types/pins.h). Nothing checks it, so an
# entry that is wrong miscompiles rather than deoptimizes. Which is why the
# omissions below are as deliberate as the entries:
#
#   - `isVector3` / `isMatrix4` / `isQuaternion` / `isEuler` are booleans.
#   - `Euler._order` is a string ('XYZ').
#   - `Quaternion._onChangeCallback` / `Euler._onChangeCallback` are functions.
#   - `Quaternion.x/y/z/w` and `Euler.x/y/z/order` are ACCESSORS over the
#     underscore fields, not slots; the underscore fields are what is pinned.
#   - `Object3D.children`, `.position`, `.matrix` and every other object- or
#     array-of-objects field are absent on purpose. Pinning those is exactly
#     what broke `mesh_churn_2k` under the blanket `BRONZE_UNSOUND_PINS` flag.

# --- Matrix3 / Matrix4: a dense 9- or 16-element array of doubles ------------
Matrix3.elements: numeric-elements
Matrix4.elements: numeric-elements

# --- Vector2 / Vector3: plain number slots -----------------------------------
Vector2.x: number
Vector2.y: number
Vector3.x: number
Vector3.y: number
Vector3.z: number

# --- Quaternion / Euler: the underscore slots the accessors front ------------
Quaternion._x: number
Quaternion._y: number
Quaternion._z: number
Quaternion._w: number
Euler._x: number
Euler._y: number
Euler._z: number
